# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown
# `CONNECTOR-IDENTITY-KEY`: a `bundle` names its members by CONNECTOR ID, which is
# the construct's own defining case — a LAG is a set of PARALLEL links between
# one pair of devices, and until now the endpoint pair could not address them
# (case 392 pins the refusal).
#
# The two member forms live in ONE comma list and are told apart by LEXIS, not
# by a flag: `--` cannot occur inside an id, so a member either contains it and
# is a pair or does not and is an id. `lag1` is the parallel case that only the
# id form reaches; `other` is the mixed list, which needs no rule of its own
# because every member resolves independently.
figdown 0.5 topology
node sw1 "Switch-1"
node sw2 "Switch-2"
node sw3 "Switch-3"
edge sw1 -- sw2 id=lag1a
edge sw1 -- sw2 id=lag1b
edge sw1 -- sw2 id=lag1c
edge sw1 -- sw3
bundle lag1 "LAG-1 (802.1AX)" lag1a,lag1b,lag1c
bundle other "Mixed" lag1a,sw1--sw3
